 A few weeks ago (just after putting a copy of 3.1.3 on my PC) Idecided 
to run a wizard. everything I got was pretty much junk, nothing special, 
except for a wand of cold.  So I decide to just go monster bashing and on 
the second level I find a shop, and on the floor of the shop (a general 
store) I find a weapon named Grayswandir. Wow... My little 1st level 
wizard gets Grayswandir from a shop? I pick it up and find out (I really 
shouldn't have been surprised) that it would cost me only 10,000 gp. only 
about 9,500 more than I had. My pet kindly walked in and pinned the shop 
keeper against the wall so I could get a good shot at him, and 3 blasts 
of the cold wand later I had a shop of junk and an uncursed +0 silver 
saber named Grayswandir.

 What I'm wondering now is how common is it to find something like this?  
It wasn't a bones level (I had a few bones levels but they were level 4+ 
and none had any artifacts) It's quite a nice object to find just laying 
around in the shops...

